pt is the bases object type() was given when it is a tuple subclass's instance (tp_bases is that object:"] [52 1 "// type(typ.__bases__) is the subclass), for the bases slice it was made with; __bases__ answers it while t's bases"] [53 1 "// are still those (type_set_bases replaces both)."] [61 1 "// basesTuple is t.__bases__: the object type() kept, else a tuple of t's bases."] [80 1 "// builtinSolid is the built-in type whose instance layout t's instances have (solid_base without the"] [81 1 "// heap types' __slots__)."] [88 13 "// a C extension's type of its base's size (extra_ivars false: arbace/pyctypes, queue 270b)"] [105 1 "// ExtMetaclass is a metaclass a C extension made (arbace/pyctypes, queue 270b): type_new defers to its tp_new."] [108 1 "// ExtAddsNoLayout is a C extension's type whose instances are its base's size (CPython's extra_ivars false: a managed"] [109 1 "// dict or weak references only), so solid_base passes over it (arbace/pyctypes, queue 270b)."] [112 1 "// solidBase is solid_base: the most derived type adding to the instance layout."] [125 1 "// unwrap is the built-in value of an instance of a class deriving from a built-in type, else o."] [133 1 "// ---- __build_class__ ----"] [136 2 "// PY5b's hooks (§7.1): the core accessors take a subclass's built-in value; a bound method of a Python"] [137 2 "// function is called by pushing its frame"] [172 1 "// dictArgs are a keyword dictionary as a call's trailing keyword arguments."] [257 38 "// not the globals' map newFrame gave a body's code (py-core-1124: test_type_aliases' test_exec_with_unusual_globals)"] [259 20 "// a dict subclass's __setitem__ sees the body's names (PY5e, part 2b)"] [290 1 "// updateBases resolves __mro_entries__ (PEP 560): the same tuple when no base has one."] [331 1 "// calculateMetaclass is _PyType_CalculateMetaclass: the most derived of meta and the bases' types."] [348 1 "// ---- type.__new__, type.__init__, type.__call__ ----"] [356 3 "// type_call's check is type's